WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.276
Scenario 4 walkthrough: Developer Productivity with Claude.

2
00:00:04.276 --> 00:00:13.620
Helping engineers explore unfamiliar code is mostly about choosing the right tool for each lookup and keeping discovery from flooding the context.

3
00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:18.463
Scenario four is an agent for developer productivity.

4
00:00:18.463 --> 00:00:25.610
Engineers use it to find their way around unfamiliar or legacy code, generate boilerplate and automate chores.

5
00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:33.341
It works with the built in tools such as Read, Grep, Glob and Edit, plus MCP servers for things like the issue tracker.

6
00:00:33.341 --> 00:00:36.524
Questions come mostly from domains two and three.

7
00:00:37.924 --> 00:00:50.058
Expect questions on picking the right built in tool, connecting MCP servers at the right scope, using plan mode and the Explore subagent, and managing context during long explorations.

8
00:00:50.058 --> 00:00:55.993
A little of domain one appears too, for example delegating focused questions to subagents.

9
00:00:57.393 --> 00:00:58.507
A common question.

10
00:00:58.507 --> 00:01:02.403
You need every place that calls a function named calculate tax.

11
00:01:02.403 --> 00:01:05.805
Glob matches file paths, so it cannot see inside files.

12
00:01:05.805 --> 00:01:09.455
Grep searches file contents, so it is the right first step.

13
00:01:09.455 --> 00:01:12.980
Then you Read the matching files to follow the call flow.

14
00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:17.681
If the function is re-exported under another name, search for that name too.

15
00:01:19.081 --> 00:01:20.072
Now a contrast.

16
00:01:20.072 --> 00:01:23.111
If only you need a server, user scope is fine.

17
00:01:23.111 --> 00:01:31.700
If the whole team should get it, configure it at project scope in the dot mcp dot json file, which is committed to the repository.

18
00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:38.175
Keep the token out of git by referencing an environment variable that each developer sets locally.

19
00:01:39.575 --> 00:01:40.471
Classic traps.

20
00:01:40.471 --> 00:01:42.711
Using Glob to search file contents.

21
00:01:42.711 --> 00:01:49.815
Retrying an Edit whose anchor is not unique instead of choosing a unique one or falling back to Read and Write.

22
00:01:49.815 --> 00:01:52.951
Scattering a team server across personal configs.

23
00:01:52.951 --> 00:01:58.903
And building a custom server for a standard integration when a maintained one already exists.

24
00:02:00.303 --> 00:02:01.555
For scenario four.

25
00:02:01.555 --> 00:02:06.079
Grep finds contents, Glob finds paths, and Read follows the flow.

26
00:02:06.079 --> 00:02:09.350
Edit needs an anchor that appears exactly once.

27
00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:15.196
Team MCP servers belong in the project config with secrets in environment variables.

28
00:02:15.196 --> 00:02:21.529
And long, noisy discovery is best delegated to a subagent so your main context stays clean.

